                "text": "Here\u2019s what the end of the Affordable Care Act\u2019s premium tax credits would mean for our SoCal community: \n\ud83d\udcb0Premiums will spike by over $2,500 annually\n\ud83d\udcc8Health care costs will rise for 35,000 people\n\ud83c\udfe59,500 CA-45 residents will lose health insurance\n\nI cosponsored the Protecting Healthcare and Lowering Costs Act to permanently extend the enhanced premium tax credit because no family should be priced out of essential care.",
